{{!
	AnnouncementBar.mustache — Blitzy component 4, the dismissible announcement band that
	sits above the floating navigation card.

	Nothing in this comment may contain a closing mustache delimiter: a comment tag ends at
	the first one, so a tag written out in full here would silently reopen the template and
	be compiled. Tags are therefore named without their braces throughout, the way the
	reference skin names them, and "the escaping form" means the ordinary double-brace
	interpolation while "the raw form" means the triple-brace one.

	INVOCATION. This partial is reached only from skin.mustache, and only from inside a
	section on data-blitzy-announcement. That enclosing section is the enable gate, and
	there is deliberately no is- flag to test in here.
	MediaWiki\Skins\Blitzy\BlitzyViewModel omits data-blitzy-announcement altogether when
	$wgBlitzyAnnounceEnable is false and when $wgBlitzyAnnounceText is empty; an absent key
	is falsy, and a falsy section renders nothing at all. A disabled bar is therefore absent
	from the document's flow rather than hidden, which is the requirement: display: none
	would leave the band in the DOM and would not comply.

	TEMPLATE DATA CONSUMED. The context inside this file is the announcement object itself,
	so its own keys are referenced unqualified rather than through a dotted path.

		string    text   Announcement body text, from $wgBlitzyAnnounceText. Always present
		                 and never empty — the view model suppresses the whole bar instead
		                 of rendering an empty band.
		string    label  Label of the action affordance, from $wgBlitzyAnnounceLabel.
		                 Always present; may be an empty string.
		string|-  href   Action target, from $wgBlitzyAnnounceLink, already accepted by
		                 MediaWiki\Skins\Blitzy\BlitzyUrlValidator. The key is ABSENT when
		                 no target was configured and when the allowlist rejected the one
		                 that was, so every use of it below sits inside a section on it.
		string    msg-blitzy-announcement-dismiss
		                 Accessible name of the dismiss control, found at the root of the
		                 template data by the parent-context walk. Declared in the messages
		                 argument of skin.json, which is what creates the key at all.

	FIXED IDENTIFIERS DEFINED HERE. resources/skins.blitzy.js/announcement.js reads both of
	them, and dismissal is a two-sided contract: the control records the dismissal, and a
	subsequent page load reads that record back and removes the band. Neither id is derived,
	suffixed or varied between renders, and the DOM order below never changes either, which
	is what keeps this band identical across every byte-compared capture.

		blitzy-announcement           the band, the element a stored dismissal removes
		blitzy-announcement-dismiss   the control that records the dismissal

	ESCAPING. This template is the single escaping site for all three configuration-sourced
	values. The view model normalises them but deliberately does not escape them: escaping
	twice would render an injected payload visibly as an entity-encoded script tag while
	still passing a naive "the payload is escaped" assertion. Every interpolation below uses
	the escaping form, and the raw form must never appear in this file.

	WHY THE ACTION AFFORDANCE SPLITS ITS TAGS. MediaWiki compiles Mustache through
	LightnCandy with FLAG_MUSTACHELOOKUP and without FLAG_PARENT, and a section opened on a
	scalar value replaces the context with that scalar without leaving the enclosing object
	on the scope stack. Two consequences shape the markup:

	  * A parent path such as ../label does not compile at all, and inside a section on href
	    a bare label or a bare href resolves to nothing. The tags are therefore split around
	    the label, so that label is read in the announcement context while the target is
	    read as the current context inside its own section. Interpolating href by name in
	    there would emit an empty href attribute on every page: a link back to the page it
	    sits on, and a defect the blocking accessibility gate would report.
	  * An empty string is truthy for a section, so no section can tell an unconfigured
	    label from a configured one. A wiki that configures a target but no label therefore
	    gets an affordance with no text; the shipped default disables the bar outright and
	    the verification instance fixes a label, so no rendered page reaches that state.

	STYLING. Every colour, radius, size and edge placement belongs to
	resources/skins.blitzy.styles/components/NavCard.less, resolved against the token
	module. This file carries class hooks only: no style attribute, no colour literal and no
	directional attribute, so the stylesheet stays free to flip for right-to-left. Two notes
	for it. The text element is a paragraph and needs its margin reset there. And the
	affordance keeps a hook of its own rather than borrowing blitzy-cta--outline from the
	navigation card, whose border differs, so that each component's computed-style assertion
	names exactly one element.
}}
<div id="blitzy-announcement" class="blitzy-announcement">
	<div class="blitzy-announcement__inner">
		<p class="blitzy-announcement__text">{{text}}</p>
		{{#href}}<a class="blitzy-announcement__action" href="{{.}}">{{/href}}{{!
		}}{{^href}}<span class="blitzy-announcement__action">{{/href}}{{!
		}}{{label}}{{!
		}}{{#href}}</a>{{/href}}{{^href}}</span>{{/href}}
		<button type="button" id="blitzy-announcement-dismiss" class="blitzy-announcement__dismiss">{{msg-blitzy-announcement-dismiss}}</button>
	</div>
</div>
